<title>ESTONIA: TALLINNA LOAN SUBSCRIPTION STARTS.</title>
<headline>TALLINNA LOAN SUBSCRIPTION STARTS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The subscription for Tallinna Pank's syndicated loan worth at least 30 million marks started on Wednesday, Tallinna Pank said.</p>
<p>The organisers of the loan, Kommerzbank and Vereins und West Bank have guaranteed 30 million marks as the loan sum, Tallinna Pank's director of financial markets, Martti Siimann told Reuters. The sum may increase if there is higher interest from the syndicate, Siimann added.</p>
<p>The syndicaters are Japanese, Scandinavian, German but also eastern European banks, Siimann said.</p>
<p>Tallinna Pank is going to use the loan to finance its growth, including the loan portfolio and the interest-bearing securities portfolio, he added.</p>
<p>Tallinna Pank will release further details on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
